A common warming-dependent decline emerges from divergent projections of tropical cyclone frequency

Cong Gao and Ning Lin
Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering, Princeton University, Princeton, NJ, USA
Correspondence: cong.gao@princeton.edu; nlin@princeton.edu

Figure scripts and input data accompanying the paper.
GFig1–GFig4 reproduce Figures 1–4; GFigS1–GFigS2 reproduce Figures S1–S2.
Each figure script is self-contained and uses the included input data.
The TSV files contain TC rates; gmt/ contains global-temperature inputs.

Requires Python 3.10+ with matplotlib, numpy, pandas, scipy, statsmodels,
xarray, netCDF4, and cftime. From this folder, run:

    for f in GFig1 GFig2 GFig3 GFig4 GFigS1 GFigS2; do python "$f.py"; done

Each script saves PDF and SVG files and opens the PDF.
See CITATION.cff for citation metadata and LICENSE for reuse terms.
The arXiv identifier and Zenodo DOI will be added when available.
